#X text 490 89 The [lop3~] object is a one-pole/one-zero filter. It has no resonance and is quite proper for this algorithm \, also because is has a good resolution for high frequencies up to nyquist. As a first order filter you have a 6 db decay per ocate \, but you can also try a 2nd order filter. Below we have a state variable filter instead with [svfilter2~]. The resonance parameter is at 0.5 \, which means no boost at the rolloff frequency. As a 2nd order \, now we have 12dB decay per octave., f 58;
